Rock Hill offers many great **youth activities for students and families**. From outdoor fun at Hargett Park to the excitement of the BMX track at Rock Hill BMX Supercross Track, young people in our community have plenty of places to gather, compete, and build friendships.

At **Resurrection Anglican Church**, we believe youth also need a place where they can grow spiritually—developing habits of faith, building meaningful friendships, and learning what it means to follow Jesus Christ in everyday life. That’s the heart behind our **youth ministry in Rock Hill, SC**.

### The G1 Club: God First

Our youth ministry, currently made up of middle school students, is called **G1 Club**. The name is simple but meaningful: **God comes first in all things**.

These years are incredibly important for spiritual formation. Our goal is to help students develop habits of faith now that will carry with them into adulthood—habits like prayer, service, friendship in Christian community, and trust in the gospel of Jesus Christ.

### Youth Activities and Community in Rock Hill

The G1 Club meets monthly for gatherings that include **fellowship, team-building activities, and service projects throughout the Rock Hill community**. Sometimes that means simply spending time together and building friendships, while other gatherings focus on serving others and learning what it means to live out our faith.

Through these shared experiences, students grow not only in friendship with one another but also in their understanding of what it means to follow Christ.

### Growing Faithful Disciples

Just as young people in Rock Hill enjoy spending time together at places like Hargett Park or riding at the Rock Hill BMX Supercross Track, our desire is for our church to be another place where youth feel welcomed, encouraged, and supported.

At **Resurrection Anglican Church**, youth ministry is about more than activities. It is about helping young people grow into **faithful and engaged disciples of Jesus Christ**—learning to love God, serve others, and live their lives with God first.

### Youth Ministry at Resurrection Anglican Church

If you are looking for **youth activities in Rock Hill, SC** or searching for a **church youth group for middle school students**, we would love to welcome your family to **Resurrection Anglican Church**.

Our prayer is that every student who joins the G1 Club will grow in friendship, faith, and a lifelong commitment to putting **God first**.
